# Initial Setup's Flight Modes page reads the vehicle's six modes and writes a change back to it.
#
# ConfigFlightModes.cs: Activate fills six combos from the mode list and sets them from FLTMODE1-6,
# the Simple boxes from the SIMPLE bitmask, and a timer lights the combo the mode channel's pulse
# selects; Save Modes writes FLTMODE1-6 and, on a copter, SIMPLE and SUPER_SIMPLE. The claim here is
# the round trip: what the page shows is what the vehicle holds, and what Save Modes writes is what
# the vehicle then holds - read back from the vehicle's own echo, not from the page.
#
# Needs SITL copter on tcp:127.0.0.1:5760 started from tools/sitl/params/copter.parm, whose
# FLTMODE1-6 are 7 9 6 3 5 0 (Circle, Land, RTL, Auto, Loiter, Stabilize), FLTMODE_CH 5 and SIMPLE 0.
# The test changes mode 2 to Loiter and ticks its Simple box, saves, checks the vehicle, then puts
# both back to copter.parm's values and checks again - so it ends where it started.

screen params
window 1600x1200
settle 6

# The page is offered once every parameter has arrived, as the C# adds it only with gotAllParams.
click param-download
settle 12
expect params.held > 1000
expect params.value.FLTMODE2 9

# SETUP opens with no page chosen and its headings closed (BackstageView.cs:261-343); the page is
# under Mandatory Hardware, which choosing opens.
click tab-setup
settle 1
expect setup.page none
expect config.flightmodes.active false
click setup-page-ConfigMandatory
click setup-page-ConfigFlightModes
settle 1
expect setup.page ConfigFlightModes
expect config.flightmodes.active true
expect config.flightmodes.firmware ArduCopter2

# What Activate read: the six modes, the mode list, the channel and the boxes.
expect config.flightmodes.1 7
expect config.flightmodes.1.name Circle
expect config.flightmodes.2 9
expect config.flightmodes.2.name Land
expect config.flightmodes.3 6
expect config.flightmodes.4 3
expect config.flightmodes.5 5
expect config.flightmodes.6 0
expect config.flightmodes.modes > 20
expect config.flightmodes.channel 5
expect config.flightmodes.pwm.label ~ 5:
expect config.flightmodes.current >= 1
expect config.flightmodes.simple 0
expect config.flightmodes.save idle

# Mode 2 to Loiter, Simple on for position 2, and save.
click fm-mode2
click fm-mode2-5
expect config.flightmodes.2 5
expect config.flightmodes.2.name Loiter
click fm-simple-2
expect config.flightmodes.simple 2
click fm-save
settle 3
expect config.flightmodes.save complete
expect params.value.FLTMODE2 5
expect params.value.SIMPLE 2
# The other five were written unchanged, so still hold what they held.
expect params.value.FLTMODE1 7
expect params.value.FLTMODE6 0

# Put them back.
click fm-mode2
click fm-mode2-9
expect config.flightmodes.2 9
click fm-simple-2
expect config.flightmodes.simple 0
click fm-save
settle 3
expect config.flightmodes.save complete
expect params.value.FLTMODE2 9
expect params.value.SIMPLE 0

# Choosing another page deactivates this one (BackstageView.cs:453-464).
click setup-page-ConfigFailSafe
expect setup.page ConfigFailSafe
expect config.flightmodes.active false
